## 1. Install procedure

### Part A — build HDT in a disposable prefix

The installer crashes against Hearthstone's real Steam prefix (7.2) but completes
reliably on a clean one. So install clean, then move the result.

```bash
export INSTALL_PREFIX="$HOME/.hdt-installer-tmp"
WINEPREFIX="$INSTALL_PREFIX" WINEARCH=win64 wineboot --init
WINEPREFIX="$INSTALL_PREFIX" winetricks -f corefonts dotnet48

# Installer from https://hsdecktracker.net/download/
WINEPREFIX="$INSTALL_PREFIX" wine HDT-Installer.exe

# Copy the result somewhere permanent.
# Real Linux username here, NOT steamuser — this is a manual prefix (2.2).
ls "$INSTALL_PREFIX/drive_c/users/$USER/AppData/Local/"   # sanity-check first
mkdir -p ~/Games
cp -r "$INSTALL_PREFIX/drive_c/users/$USER/AppData/Local/HearthstoneDeckTracker" ~/Games/HDT
rm -rf "$INSTALL_PREFIX"
```

This produces a complete Squirrel layout, which is what HDT requires:

```
~/Games/HDT/
├── app-<version>/
├── packages/          (RELEASES + full .nupkg)
├── Update.exe
└── HearthstoneDeckTracker.exe   ← top-level shim
```

### Part B — prepare Hearthstone's real Steam prefix

Start Hearthstone through Steam, leave it running, then:

```bash
PID=$(pgrep -f Hearthstone.exe) || echo "Hearthstone is not running"
ENVFILE=$(tr '\0' '\n' < /proc/$PID/environ)
export WINEPREFIX=$(grep  '^WINEPREFIX='       <<<"$ENVFILE" | cut -d= -f2-)
export PROTON_WINE=$(grep '^PROTON_DIST_PATH=' <<<"$ENVFILE" | cut -d= -f2-)/bin/wine
export HS_APPID=$(basename "$(dirname "$WINEPREFIX")")
echo "$WINEPREFIX"; echo "$PROTON_WINE"; echo "$HS_APPID"

WINE="${PROTON_WINE}" winetricks -f corefonts dotnet48
WINE="${PROTON_WINE}" winetricks msdelta

# Verify — do NOT trust winetricks' own success messages (2.3, 3):
ls "${WINEPREFIX}/drive_c/windows/Microsoft.NET/Framework64/v4.0.30319/WPF/wpfgfx_v0400.dll"
ls "${WINEPREFIX}/drive_c/windows/system32/msdelta.dll"
```

`protontricks "${HS_APPID}" -f corefonts dotnet48` and
`protontricks "${HS_APPID}" msdelta` are equivalent.

### Part C — launch

```bash
cd ~/Games/HDT
WINEPREFIX="${WINEPREFIX}" "${PROTON_WINE}" "HearthstoneDeckTracker.exe"
```

HDT's own updater now keeps itself current on every launch, entirely under Wine.
No external update script. Launch HDT **after** Hearthstone is confirmed running.

