## 6. Common wrong answers — never suggest these

| Suggestion | Why it's wrong |
|---|---|
| "You need Windows to install HDT" | False. See Section 1 |
| Copy `Update.exe` from a Windows install | Obsolete — the installer produces it on Linux |
| Run `HDT-Installer.exe` against the Steam prefix | Reliably crashes (7.2) |
| `dotnet45` / `dotnet462` / `dotnet472` alone, or Wine-Mono | Insufficient for HDT's WPF UI (2.3) |
| Trust winetricks' "already installed, skipping" | Known false positive (2.3) |
| Bare `winetricks msdelta` with no prefix set | Targets `~/.wine`; can damage a Proton prefix (2.4) |
| Poll `HearthSim/Hearthstone-Deck-Tracker` releases for the latest build | Portable zips were discontinued in v1.56.0; that repo is capped at v1.55.6 forever. Real channel is `HearthSim/HDT-Releases` |
| Extract a `-full.nupkg` and run the exe from it | No `Update.exe` — incomplete layout, crashes (7.1) |
| Hardcode a Steam AppID for Hearthstone | Per-install and hash-derived (2.1) |
| Launch concurrent apps through Lutris or Bottles | Wrapper-level block (2.5) |
| Blame WinRT / `RoGetParameterizedTypeInstanceIID` | Investigated and disproven; those trace lines are coincidental |
| Set `COMPlus_*` variables (gcServer, TieredCompilation, AVX2, etc.) | Tested individually and combined — no effect |
| Blame the .NET version or ReadyToRun | Prefix had 4.8 (exceeds the 4.7.2 minimum); no R2R markers in any build |
| Disable HDT hardware acceleration for overlay issues | Obsolete — fixed upstream in v1.56.3 |
| Focus-follows-mouse, or `xdotool` override-redirect, for overlay clicks | Made things worse / broke other fixes |
| Shadow `xdg-open` on `PATH` to fix login | Tested, unreliable |
| Tell a plain-Wine user login works without the Steam sandbox | It fails there too (5) |
| Bundle `msdelta.dll` in a repo | Microsoft-licensed (2.4) |
| File a Wine bug for msdelta | The stub is known and intentional; the winetricks override is the supported workaround |

