## 7. Unsolved bugs

Both report `80131506`, but that's the CLR's generic unrecoverable-fault code, **not
evidence of a shared cause** — they're different executables. Neither blocks
anything; Section 1 sidesteps both.

**7.1 Bare app exe with no `packages/` folder** crashes with `80131506`, unaffected
by `msdelta`, no unimplemented-function message. Untested candidates:
`SquirrelInit()`'s `new UpdateManager("INVALID_PATH")`, or `SentryReporter.Initialize()`
(the Sentry SDK replaced SharpRaven after v1.56.0 and wasn't in the last working
portable build). *Cheap unrun test:* check whether
`.../AppData/Roaming/HearthstoneDeckTracker/Logs/hdt_log.txt` is created — HDT's
first log write is inside `Core.Initialize()`, the last startup call.
**Workaround:** install via Part A.

**7.2 Installer against the real Steam prefix** crashes with `80131506`, no msdelta
reference in the logs. Ruled out: `msdelta`, stale `mscoree=native` override,
leftover install folders. The distinguishing variable seems to be prefix age or
accumulated state. Reproduced on one long-used prefix only; behaviour on a fresh
Steam prefix is unknown. **Workaround:** Part A.

**7.3 Installer via a Steam non-Steam-game shortcut** (with `STEAM_COMPAT_DATA_PATH`
redirected) hangs before producing any log output — earlier than direct `wine`
invocation fails. Possibly a `pressure-vessel` interaction. Direct `wine` invocation
is the only reliable launch method.

**7.4 Login outside the Steam sandbox** — see Section 5. This is the only unsolved
item that still costs something.

**7.5 Untested escape hatch:** the source tree still has a non-Squirrel build
config (`Release|x64` omits the `SQUIRREL` define). Building it would avoid the
Squirrel path entirely, sidestepping 7.1 and 7.2 — at the cost of auto-update. A
fork can build it on a GitHub Actions `windows-latest` runner, so no local Windows
is needed.

